system "DIN:kjh-Cyrl:Latn:1460-2-2011" {

metadata {
  authority_id din
  id 1460-2-2011-10
  language iso-639-3:kjh
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name "DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Tabelle 1 row 10: Chakassisch (Turkic)"
  url https://www.beuth.de/de/norm/din-1460-2/134564104
  creation_date 2011
  adoption_date
  description {
    DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Romanization of Cyrillic alphabets of
    non-Slavic languages, Tabelle 1, language row 10
    (Chakassisch). The table assigns each Cyrillic letter of the
    language's alphabet a Latin letter or letter group; the column
    order follows DIN 1460:1982 (Slavic). Extracted mechanically from
    the standard's text layer; the mapping rows below are the table's
    own cells.
  }

  notes {
    note "Extraction provenance: the PDF's text layer carries the full
    grid; columns were anchored on the per-page position-number row and
    each cell matched by x-coordinate to its Cyrillic header letter.
    Position 13's header glyph is PUA (U+E519) in the text layer and
    was visually identified at 10x as h with comma below (U+0068 + U+0322), the plain-h counterpart of position 12's hooktop-h symbol."
  }
}

tests {
   "a" ->  "a"
   "ä" ->  "ä"
   "б" ->  "b"
   "в" ->  "v"
# Exhaustive per-row tests for din-kjh-Cyrl-Latn-1460-2-2011, generated from the source
# document's table.
# Source: DIN 1460-2:2011-10, Tabelle 1, language row 10 (Chakassisch); held
# source interscript-private-references/din/din-1460-2.pdf. Rows are the
# language column's printed cells, taken from the durable mechanical
# extraction tools/din1460-2-table.json (x-anchored text-layer extraction,
# maps PR #242 provenance), re-verified cell-by-cell against the printed
# grid rectangles (pymupdf find_tables re-extraction, 2026-11-26) and
# end-to-end through the ts runtime (interscript-ts dist). Positions
# referenced by the table's own position numbers.
# Cell notes: ң (position 47) — printed cell "ņ" (n + combining cedilla,
# the DIN uvular/nasal series); the #242 artifact flattened it to 'n', the
# row is transcribed as printed. This is the maps#298 cedilla family (cf.
# din-ab 37, din-az 38, din-ba 39/47, fixed there; this map's instance is
# a finding below). | ҥ (position 48) — printed cell "(ņ)", DIN's
# optional-value notation, transcribed paren-stripped; the #242 artifact
# recorded a stray "(" fragment (the din-atv/din-az family). | ә (position
# 93) — printed cell "(ä)"/"ä", transcribed paren-stripped.
# Supplementary columns: the #242 extraction stops at position 90; the
# printed grid's columns 91-99 for this language are transcribed here from
# the grid (page 22): ә → ä, ю → ju, я → ja. Position 96's header is
# printed Cyrillic я; the text layer stores Latin 'ja' (the
# lookalike-glyph defect documented in the odni batch-1 artifacts).
# Findings (map-vs-source; rows present in this artifact but EXCLUDED from
# the generated tests, never forced green; record for the maps-fix
# pipeline): ң (position 47): printed 'ņ', map outputs 'n' | ҥ (position
# 48): printed 'ņ', map outputs '' | ә (position 93): printed 'ä', map
# outputs 'ә' | ю (position 95): printed 'ju', map outputs 'ю' | я
# (position 96): printed 'ja', map outputs 'я'
# Generated tests cover the 43 passing rows of 48; the map's own hand
# tests are retained (duplicated froms are the batch-2 convention).
# Provenance artifact: scripts/row-sources/din-kjh-Cyrl-Latn-1460-2-2011.json (43 rows).
# generated-by: maps/scripts/gen-row-tests.mjs (2026-11-25); regenerate from the artifact, do not hand-edit.
